# What `s[i]` yields: a one-character string counted in code points, on both backends (ADR 0225).
# The row this came from was L11.5's byte-index debt -- `"abc"[1]` answered 98 and the compiled leg
# refused the variable case outright. Note that the *index* is code-point correct on both legs even
# where the compiled `len` of non-ASCII text is not (Gap R.47). CPython prints exactly this.
print("abc"[1])
s = "héllo"
print(s[0])
print(s[4])
